<h1>50cc Motorbike Hanoi: First-time Visitors Parking</h1>
<p>Parking is the skill no first-time visitor expects to need and the one Hanoi demands a dozen times a day. The city parks its motorbikes nose to kerb, row behind row, on sidewalks and in attended lots, and a visitor's day is scored less by the rides between stops than by the twenty-meter maneuvers at each one. The verified rate for a 50cc scooter is 200,000 VND per day, the shop sits at 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, and a first rental day on a 50cc includes parking practice whether you planned for it or not. This page plans for it.</p>
<p>It belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/">50cc motorbike rental hub for Hanoi</a> and pairs with our guide on <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/50cc-scooter-rental-for-beginners-hanoi/">renting a 50cc scooter as a beginner in Hanoi</a>. For what a rental costs across the lineup, the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost overview</a> lists every verified price, and the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> answers the counter questions we hear most from visitors on their first trip. This page handles the parking half of the day.</p>
